# .gitignore template — the secrets-out-of-git wall (guide/06-secrets.md)
#
# Strategy: ALLOWLIST for sensitive areas — deny everything, then un-ignore only
# the specific known-safe files. Fails CLOSED: a new file near secrets is excluded
# until you deliberately allow it. Copy to your repo root as .gitignore and adapt.

# ── Hard-exclude secret shapes, everywhere, permanently ─────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*
**/*.kdbx                 # vault files
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json

# ── Credential/auth directories for your tools (add yours) ──────────────────
# .config/<tool>/auth/
# .<tool>/credentials

# ── Config-manager local data (holds node identity) ─────────────────────────
chezmoi.toml
.chezmoi.toml.local

# ── Allowlist pattern for a sensitive directory ─────────────────────────────
# Deny-all the dir, then un-ignore ONLY known-safe files:
#
#   sensitive-dir/*
#   !sensitive-dir/                 # keep the dir itself trackable
#   !sensitive-dir/README.md        # a safe file, explicitly allowed
#   !sensitive-dir/config.example   # placeholders only, no real values
#
# Never un-ignore an .env, a *.kdbx, or a *token* file back in.

# ── OS / editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
